What:		/proc/jank_info/cpu_jank_info/ux_throttle
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	4.14.357-openela-miru-h40
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only ColorOS 14 UX execution-budget telemetry.  The file emits
		64 records followed by a blank line.  Records use the OnePlus 9R
		field grammar:

		pid,comm,realtime_seconds.realtime_nanoseconds,cpu,current_khz,max_khz

		The 4 ms base budget and the donor's light, heavy, animator,
		list-pick, launch-scene, and system-server lock-owner multipliers are
		preserved.  Runtime is sampled from the native 4.14 scheduler tick,
		but only for the at-most-four PIDs selected through task_track while
		task_track_enable is nonzero.  Records and accounting use fixed-size
		storage; the normal unarmed path performs only two lock-free checks.

		This telemetry port does not replace H.40's established UX task-pick
		policy with the newer SM8250 scheduler implementation.
Users:		ColorOS performance diagnostics compatible with the OnePlus 9R
		Android 14 CPU-jank ABI.
